# AES(Advanced Encryption Standard) Algorithm

AES is a symmetric-key encryption algorithm widely used for protecting data.

Implementation
Language: Java
Algorithm: AES
Mode: ECB
Padding: PKCS5Padding
Key: Generated from a secret string using SHA-1
Key Size: 128-bit
Encoding: Base64
Operation: Encryption and Decryption

The program encrypts a sample URL using a secret key and then decrypts it to obtain the original URL.
